Configure your identity
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

What does --global mean? Git supports configuration at different levels.
| Level | Scope | Example |
|---|---|---|
| System | All users on the computer | System-wide Git settings |
| Global | Your user account | Your default commit identity |
| Local | The current repository | A project-specific identity |

