What if you forget to create a branch?
Suppose you make several employee-creation changes while still on main.

If the changes are uncommitted, you can often create a branch immediately:

git switch -c feature/add-employee
The uncommitted changes normally remain in your working tree.

But if you have already committed the feature directly to main, creating a new branch from the current main will not separate those commits from main.


